![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Using `Get-Volume` to find used drive letters can miss network mapped drives, subst drives, or other virtual drives that occupy a drive letter but are not managed by the Storage Management API. Using `[System.IO.DriveInfo]::GetDrives()` is more robust as it queries all active logical drives directly from the OS.

```
    $used = [System.IO.DriveInfo]::GetDrives() | ForEach-Object { $_.Name[0] }
    foreach ($candidate in [char[]]'ZYXWVUTSRQPONMLKJIHGFED') {
        if ($used -notcontains $candidate) { return [string]$candidate }
    }
```

